          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            This page describes a proposal for a formalization of the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            – supposedly a natural process that turns the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian"} local Lagrangian
            data of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher algebraic
            data of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+quantum+field+theory"} local quantum field theory
            – formulated in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} cohesive (∞,1)-toposes
          %p The fundamental observation here is that is natural to
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                (
                %strong> prequantum fields
                ) – identify spaces of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
                as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
                of higher
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stacks"} moduli stacks
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} base (∞,1)-topos
            %li
              %p
                (
                %strong> local action functionals
                ) – identify
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functionals"} local action functionals
                as lifts of these
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
                to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice
                of the base
                = succeed "-topos" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group+of+units"} ∞-group of units
                of a suitable
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
                object
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %li
              %p
                (
                %strong> path integral
                ) – identify the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
                of these local action functionals on spaces of trajectories as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral+as+a+pull-push+transform"} pull-push operation
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
