          %p
            But even with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            restricted to be of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mi Mod
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo □
                        %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Mod^{\Box^n}
            or similar, the notion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            as above is still much more general than the field theories typically of interest in nature and in theory. The quantum field theories actually of interest both in nature and in theory have the special property that they arise via a process of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometric data
            given by a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+Lagrangian"} local Lagrangian
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space"} moduli space
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
          %p This is the process to be indicated in the following:
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
