          %h3#ExpositionLocalPrequantumFieldTheory 2. Local prequantum field theory
          %p
            First we consider
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"} Nuiten 13, section 2
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FiorenzaRogersSchreiber13a"} Fiorenza-Rogers-Schreiber 13a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#lpqft"} Nuiten-Schreiber 13
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            The notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            is often said to be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom"} axiomatized
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundle"} fiber bundle
            over
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            – called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/true"} true
            for simple instances of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scalar+fields"} scalar fields
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            fields.
          %p
            But it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            as in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            (and is ever more false for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            or in the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            regarded as a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of a kind of bundle whose fiber is the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton+sector"} instanton sector
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}(\nabla)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            is still a section of a bundle whose typical fiber is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
            one has:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %msub
                            %mi G
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∇
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mi U
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi c
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo ∇
                              %msub
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla|_U}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  U &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{c}(\nabla|_U)}{\to}&amp;
                  \\mathbf{B}G
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is not a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+groupoid"} smooth groupoid
            (a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+stack"} geometric stack
            = succeed "-fiber" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbf{B}G)
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} fiber 2-bundle
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+object+in+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Here the
            = succeed "-nature" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is a precise reflection of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+principle"} gauge principle
            governing the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
          %p
            Similarly, an abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+field"} n-form gauge field
            (e.g. the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity+C-field"} supergravity C-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli n-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} smooth n-groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
            for these is hence a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-gerbe"} n-gerbe
          %p
            (All this is true in the complete
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            description of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            approximation. Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+differentiation"} Lie differentiation
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-stack"} smooth higher stack
            is precisely an
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebroid"} L-∞ algebroid
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            (only) one may generally assume (mostly) that fields are indeed sections of an ordinary
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+bundle"} field bundle
          %p
            So in order to formalize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            one needs to pair
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} geometric ∞-groupoids
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometry
                +
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                \=
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} ∞-topos
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
                +
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+theory"} higher
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
                \=
                = succeed "/" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} geometric ∞-groupoid
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
                \.
          %p
            We consider now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            to be a suitable such
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothSuper%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SmoothSuper∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Sh
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi SuperManifolds
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mi lhe
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Supermanifolds
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi KanComplexes
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coloneqq Sh_\infty(SuperManifolds) = L_{lhe} Func(Supermanifolds^{op}, KanComplexes)
          %p
            which is the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            for the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boson"} bosonic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            and of higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            (for the description of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
          %p
            More generally, for constructing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stacks"} moduli ∞-stacks
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+fields"} higher gauge fields
            we need an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            that satisfies an axiom called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesion"} cohesion
          %p
            Given such
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stack"} moduli ∞-stack
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} \in \mathbf{H}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
            is regarded as
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a map
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\phi \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow \mathbf{Fields}
              %p
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
                of such fields is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
                betwen two such maps,
            %li
              %p
                and a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+gauge+transformation"} higher gauge transformation
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+homotopy"} higher homotopy
                between those.
          %p
            With physical fields in hand, next we need to axiomatize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            of such fields.
          %p
            Now a space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            of fields is itself a space of fields, together with projections to the incoming and the outgoing fields configurations, hence a
            = succeed "-shaped" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} trajectories
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                  %mi in
                          %mover
                            %mo ↙
                            %mrow
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi out
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mi in
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mi out
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{Fields}_{\mathrm{trajectories}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;   {}^{\mathllap{(-)|_{in}}}\stackrel{}{\swarrow}
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\searrow^{\mathrlap{(-)_{out}}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{Fields}_{in}
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                  \\mathbf{Fields}_{out}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            We say that this is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            (or in fact a
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                higher
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi in
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{in}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                      %mi out
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{out}
          %p For instance for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Σ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↖
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi in
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi out
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma_{in}
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                  \\Sigma_{out}
                  }
          %p
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
            with incoming and outgoing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            as indicated, and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            as above, then forming
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+stacks"}> mapping stacks
            ) yields the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Fields
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi in
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Fields
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi out
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi Fields
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; [\Sigma,\, \mathbf{Fields}]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  [\partial_{in}\Sigma,\, \mathbf{Fields}]
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                  [\partial_{out} \Sigma,\, \mathbf{Fields}]
                  }
          %p
            which exhibits field configurations on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            as trajectories along which fields on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi in
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_{in} \Sigma
            propagate to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi out
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_{out} \Sigma
          %p
            In the example here,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            is the moduli of some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            field (hence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo =
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} = X
            a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            of shape the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi in
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_{in}
            coming in, propagating and interacting along a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            of shape
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi out
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_{out}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+process"} scattering process
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            will be what is called the corresponding
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering+amplitude"} scattering amplitude
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+amplitude"} probability amplitude
            for the process to take place) or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+function"} n-point function
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlator"} correlator
          %p
            Specifying the example further, suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k+1)
            disjoint
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/balls"} balls
            marked, regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↖
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %munderover
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                            %mi k
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mi d
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi D
                            %mi d
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; S^d
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                  \\\
                  \\coprod_{i = 1}^k D^d
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                  D^d
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            then For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            fields this may be taken to encode a diagram where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %em
              open
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            come in, merge, and one comes out. For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 1
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 3
            this is a cobordism that when “viewed in time direction” is an inclusion of three small intervals into one larger interval
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                      %mo [
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ]
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi in
                            %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ]
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi in
                            %mn 2
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mrow
                          %mo [
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ]
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi in
                            %mn 3
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ]
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi out
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left[
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\left[ \;\;\;\;\; \right]_{\Sigma_{in}^1}
                  \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                  \\left[ \;\; \right]_{\Sigma_{in}^2}
                  \\;\;\;\;
                  \\left[ \;\;\;\; \right]_{\Sigma_{in}^3}
                  \\;\;\;
                  \\right]_{\Sigma_{out}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            These are of course the operations in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/little+k-cubes+operad"} little k-cubes operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of local boundary prequantum field theory restricted to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            of this form yields what are called topological or
            %em locally constant
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/factorization+algebras"} factorization algebras
          %p
            To capture all this functorially, write then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_n(\mathbf{H})^\otimes
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+of+n-fold+correspondences"} (∞,n)-category of n-fold correspondences
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            are those of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            between them, as above. This is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
            by objectwise
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
          %p One finds that:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em every
                object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
                is self-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+dualizable+object"} fully dualizable
                in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Corr
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_n(\mathbf{H})^\otimes
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+trace"} higher trace
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi tr
                        %mrow
                          %mi Π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Σ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tr_{\Pi(\Sigma)}(\mathbf{Fields})
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape"} shape
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Σ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(\Sigma)
                of this
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+dualizable+object"} fully dualizable object
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stack"} moduli ∞-stack
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+modality"} flat
                fields on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                – this is the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
                of fields (for fields of
                = succeed "-type" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            This means, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stack"} moduli ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields} \in \mathbf{H}
            is equivalently a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-functor"} monoidal (∞,n)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{Fields}
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Bord_n^\otimes
                  \\longrightarrow
                  Corr_n(\mathbf{H})^\otimes
          %p
            which sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordisms"} cobordisms
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            between in- and out-going flat field configurations over the boundary, given by flat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectories"} trajectories
            over the cobordism:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↖
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi in
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi out
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mover
                    %mo ↦
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mi in
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                    %mi out
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi in
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mi Π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi out
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \nearrow &amp;&amp; \nwarrow
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma_{in}
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                  \\Sigma_{out}
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\;\;
                  \\stackrel{\;\;\;\;\;\;}{\mapsto}
                  \\;\;
                  \\left(
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; [\Pi(\Sigma), \mathbf{Fields}]
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{(-)|_{in}}}\swarrow
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \\searrow^{\mathrlap{(-)|_{out}}}
                  \\\
                  [\Pi(\Sigma_{in}), \mathbf{Fields}]
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  \&amp;&amp;
                  [\Pi(\Sigma_{out}), \mathbf{Fields}]
                  }
                  \\right)
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this way the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+%E2%88%9E-stack"} moduli ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            encodes the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinematics"} kinematics
            of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
          %p
            Next we define the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            by defining a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
            which assigns to each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectory"} trajectory
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+amplitude"} probability amplitude
            for that trajectory to be “physically realized”.
          %p
            Traditionally, in non-localized
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is a map of the form
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fields
                      %mi traj
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{traj} \longrightarrow U(1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi traj
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{traj} \coloneqq [S^1, X]
            the smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that is equipped with a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla \colon X \to \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
            (an
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holonomy"} holonomy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonlinear+functional"} functional
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hol
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hol_\nabla \colon [S^1, X] \to U(1)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            term for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particle"} charged particle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+model"} sigma model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            To see how this is axiomatized in
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+field+theory"} local
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mn 0
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mn 0
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; U(1)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \swArrow_\simeq &amp;&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{0}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{0}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            (as a
            = succeed "!)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ω
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)\simeq \Omega \mathbf{B}U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            construction, this means that maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Fields
                    %mi traj
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}_{traj} \longrightarrow U(1)
            are equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
                            %mi traj
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
