                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr_n\left(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}}\right)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            in the slice contains trajectories equipped with action functionals.
          %p
            In conclusion, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i S)
            on a species
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} physical fields
            is a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i S)
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Bord
                            %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi exp
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mi S
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Corr
                            %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi H
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %msup
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi B
                                    %mi n
                                  %mi U
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⊗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi Fields
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Corr
                            %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi H
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Bord_n^\otimes
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\exp(i S)}{\to}&amp;
                  Corr_n\left(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)}\right)^\otimes
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{Fields}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; Corr_n\left(\mathbf{H}\right)^\otimes
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Such a diagram defines a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field+theory"}> topological
            +
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"}> boundary
            +
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defect+field+theory"}> defects
            ).
          %p
            This theory may have boundaries/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"}> branes
            \. Below we find that most
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+quantum+field+theories"} local quantum field theories
            of interest arise actually as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theories"} boundary field theories
            of a higher dimensional field theory and that their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            is induced from that higher dimensional theory in a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"}> holographic
            ” way that generalizes the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS3-CFT2+and+CS-WZW+correspondence"} AdS3-CFT2 and CS-WZW correspondence
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Bord
                    %mi n
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n^\otimes
            is generated precisely from one boundary brane of top
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            is equivalent to specifying a boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fields
