            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunctions"} wavefunctions
            to the outgoing ones.
          %h3#ExpositionCohomologicalQuantization 4. Cohomological quantization by pull-push
          %p
            We now survey the cohomological quantization step. See (
            %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"}> Nuiten 13, section 4
            ).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            What we need now for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            map that adds up the values of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            over the space of trajectories, a functor of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %msup
                    %mi Mod
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo □
                        %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int (-)
                  \\;\;
                  \\colon
                  \\;\;
                  Corr_n\left(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)}\right)^\otimes
                  \\to
                  (E Mod^{\Box^n})^\otimes
          %p
            As such this will in general only exist for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} ∞-Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Fields
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Fields}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
            and hence has a “counting measure”. This case has been considered in (
            %a{:href => "#FreedHopkinsLurieTeleman09"}> Freed-Hopkins-Lurie-Teleman 09
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Morton10"} Morton 10
          %p
            In the general case the path integral requires that we
            %em choose
            a suitable
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            on the spaces of fields. We see below what this means, for the moment we just write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi n
                    %mi or
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi n
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Corr^{or}_n(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)})^\otimes
          %p
            (i.e. with an
            = succeed "-superscript)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi or
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {(-)}^{or}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} (∞,n)-category
            of suitably oriented/measured spaces of fields with action functional. Then we may consider lifts of the action functional to
            %em measure-valued
            action functionals
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi n
                    %mi or
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi E
                      %msup
                        %mi Mod
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo □
                            %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(i S) \, d\mu
                  \\;\colon\;
                  Corr_n^{or}\left(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)}\right)^\otimes
                  \\to
                  \\left(
                  E Mod^{\Box^n}
                  \\right)^\otimes
                  \\,.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            is then to be a monoidal functor of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∫
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Corr
                    %mi n
                    %mi or
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi E
                      %msup
                        %mi Mod
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mo □
                            %mi n
                      %mo )
                    %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int(-) \;\colon\;
                  Corr_n^{or}\left(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)}\right)^\otimes
                  \\to
                  \\left(
                  E Mod^{\Box^n}
                  \\right)^\otimes
                  \\,.
          %p
            This we discuss now below. Once we have such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            functor, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            process is its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            with the given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi μ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i S) \, d \mu
            to obtain the genuine quantized
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo ∈
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Fields
                          %mi exp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi d
                          %mi μ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Bord
                            %mi n
                            %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi exp
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mi S
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi d
                              %mi μ
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Corr
                            %mi n
                            %mi or
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %msub
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi H
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %msup
                                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                      %mi B
                                    %mi n
                                  %mi U
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⊗
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∫
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi E
                              %msup
                                %mi Mod
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mo □
                                    %mi n
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⊗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi Fields
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Corr
                            %mi n
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi H
                              %mo )
                            %mo ⊗
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\underset{\phi \in \mathbf{Fields}}{\int}
                  \\exp(i S(\phi)) \, d \mu(\phi)
                  \&amp;
                  \\colon
                  \&amp;
                  Bord_n^\otimes
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\exp(i S)\, d\mu}{\to}&amp;
                  Corr_n^{or}\left(\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}^n U(1)}\right)^\otimes
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\int (-) }{\to}&amp;
                  \\left(
                  E Mod^{\Box^n}
                  \\right)^\otimes
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp; {}_{\mathllap{Fields}}\searrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; Corr_n\left(\mathbf{H}\right)^\otimes
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            We realize this now by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} fiber integration in generalized cohomology
          %p
            While traditionally the definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            is notoriously elusive, here we make use of general abstract but basic facts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+linear+algebra"} higher linear algebra
            in a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tensor (∞,1)-category
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
          %p
            %em Cohomological integration
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  Fiber integration of
                  = succeed "-modules" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphisms"} dual morphisms
                of pulling back
                = succeed "-modules." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi E
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %li
              %p
                The choice of
                %em measure
                against which one integrates is the choice of identification of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
          %p
            More in detail, given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⊗
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^\otimes
            and given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f \;\colon\; V_1 \to V_2
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration"}> fiber integration
              \/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"}> push-forward
              \/
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index map
            is just
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                forming the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo ∨
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %msubsup
                          %mi V
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ∨
                        %mo →
                        %msubsup
                          %mi V
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ∨
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\vee \colon V_2^\vee \to V_1^\vee
            %li
              %p
                such that
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalences"} equivalences
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∨
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_i^\vee \simeq V_i
                exhibiting self-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
                exist (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"}> Poincaré duality
                ) and have been chosen (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"}> orientation
                ).
          %p This allows in total to have a morphism between the same objects, but in the opposite direction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi V
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ∨
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∨
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msubsup
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∨
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ≃
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^!
                  \\;\colon\;
                  V_2
                  \\stackrel{\;\simeq\;}{\to}
                  V_2^\vee
                  \\stackrel{\; f^\vee \;}{\to}
                  V_1^\vee
                  \\stackrel{\; \simeq \;}{\to}
                  V_1
                  \\,.
          %p
            That this is also the mechanism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} fiber integration in generalized cohomology
            is almost explicit in the literature (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander-Whitehead-Atiyah+duality"}> Alexander-Whitehead-Atiyah duality
            ), if maybe not fully clearly so. The statement is discussed explicitly in (
            %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"}> Nuiten 13, section 4.1
            ).
          %p
            First, the basic example to keep in mind is integration in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                  %mo =
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = H R = H \mathbb{C}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a manifold, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spectrum"} mapping spectrum
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H R^\bullet(X)
                  \\coloneqq
                  [X,H R]
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré duality
            asserts that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi H
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H R^\bullet(X) \in H R Mod
            is essentially a self-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"}> dual object
            , except for a shift in degree: a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            induces an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo •
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi X
                    %mo )
                  %munderover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi PD
                        %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi H
                      %msup
                        %mi R
                        %mrow
                          %mo •
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                          %mi dim
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi X
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∨
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mi X
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H R^\bullet\left(X\right)
                  \\underoverset{\simeq}{\;\; PD_X\;\;}{\to}
                  \\left(
                  H R^{\bullet+ dim(X)}\left(X\right)\right)^\vee
                  \\simeq
                  H R_{\bullet + dim(X)}\left(X\right)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Using this, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to Y
            a map of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifolds"} closed manifolds
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            of both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            induces from the canonical push-forward map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\ast
            on homology the
            = succeed "/push-forward" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Umkehr+map"} Umkehr map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi PD
                        %mi X
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi H
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %munderover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msubsup
                        %mi PD
                        %mi Y
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f^!
                  \=
                  \\int_f
                  \\;\colon\;
                  H R^\bullet(X)
                  \\underoverset{\simeq}{\;PD_X\;}{\to}
                  H R_{\bullet + dim(X)}(X)
                  \\stackrel{\; f_\ast \;}{\to}
                  H R_{\bullet + dim(X)}(Y)
                  \\underoverset{\simeq}{\;PD_Y^{-1}\;}{\to}
                  H R^{n-(dim(X)-dim(Y))}(Y)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is ordinary
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration"} integration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mathbb{R}^\bullet(X)
            is modeled by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi PD
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PD_X
            is given by a choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^! = \int_{f}
            is ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+of+differential+forms"} integration of differential forms
          %p
            The shift in degree here seems to somewhat break the simple pattern. In fact this is not so, if only we realize that since we are working over spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em relative/fiberwise
            point of view and regard not duality in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Mod
            itself, but in the functor categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(X, E Mod)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E Mod
          %p
            Accordingly, given an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-module+bundle"} (∞,1)-module bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi \;\colon \;  X \to E Mod
          %p
            we form not just the mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet(X) = [X, E]
            as above, but form the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            of this bundle, which we write:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E^{\bullet + \chi}(X) \coloneqq \Gamma_X(\chi)
          %p
            Here for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} discrete ∞-groupoid
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo →
                  %mi χ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Gamma_X(\chi) \coloneqq [\underset{\to}{\lim} \chi, E]
                  \\,.
          %p Consider now a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo *
                                %mi χ
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi χ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;&amp; \stackrel{f}{\to} &amp;&amp; Y
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{f^\ast \chi}}\searrow &amp;\swArrow&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\chi}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; E Mod
                  }
          %p
            along which we want to integrate, whith
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            invertible in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(Y, E Mod)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi χ
                          %mo ∨
                        %mo )
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\chi^\vee\right)^\vee \simeq \chi
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %msup
                          %mi χ
                          %mo ∨
                        %mo )
                      %mo ∨
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left(\chi^\vee\right)^\vee \simeq \chi
          %p
            Observe that we have the pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triples"} adjoint triples
            of left/right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extensions"} Kan extensions
            and
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Func
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi E
                          %mi Mod
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo *
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo !
                        %mtd
                          %mi Func
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mi E
                          %mi Mod
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mover
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo *
                              %mover
                                %mo ←
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo *
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mo !
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y &amp;\stackrel{p}{\to}&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \\\
                  Func(X, E Mod)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\overset{f_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{f^\ast}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{f_\ast}{\to}}}
                  \&amp;
                  Func(Y, E Mod)
                  \&amp;\stackrel{\overset{p_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{p^\ast}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{p_\ast}{\to}}}
                  \&amp;
                  E Mod
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast
            preserves duals, but
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            may not.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ∨
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_! f^\ast \chi^\vee
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualizable+object"} dualizable object
            %em choice of twisted orientation
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            is a choice of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi β
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta \colon X \to E Mod
            together with a choice of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            (if such exists) of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PD
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ∨
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∨
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi χ
                    %mo +
                    %mi β
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  PD
                  \\;\colon \;
                  \\left( f_! f^\ast \chi^\vee
                  \\right)^\vee
                  \\simeq
                  f_!\left(
                  f^\ast \chi + \beta
                  \\right)
                  \\,,
          %p
            hence a choice of correction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_!
            preserving the duality of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^\ast \chi
          %p
            Then the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mo ⊣
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f_! \dashv f^\ast)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ∨
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ∨
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f_! f^\ast \chi^\vee \to  \chi^\vee
          %p
            induces the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+morphism"} dual morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mo !
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msup
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ∨
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∨
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi PD
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mo !
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi χ
                    %mo +
                    %mi β
                    %mo )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\chi
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\left(f_! f^\ast \chi^\vee \right)^\vee
                  \\underoverset{\simeq}{PD}{\longrightarrow}
                  f_!\left(
                  f^\ast \chi + \beta
                  \\right)
          %p
            and under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left[ p_! \left( - \right), E \right]
            this becomes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo !
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi χ
                      %mo +
                      %mi β
                      %mo )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mo !
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left[p_! f_! \left(f^\ast \chi + \beta\right), E\right]
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\left[p_! \chi , E\right]
          %p which is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi f
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %mi χ
                      %mo +
                      %mi β
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\int_f
                  \\;\colon \;
                  E^{\bullet + f^\ast \chi + \beta}(X)
                  \\longrightarrow
                  E^{\bullet + \chi}(Y)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This we may call the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+generalized+cohomology"} fiber integration
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %em
              twisted
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
              map
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %em
              , induced by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi β
                      %mo ,
                      %mi PD
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\beta, PD)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi β
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta = 0
              then we call
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PD
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PD
              an
            = succeed "_" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
          %p Notice that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Under fiber integration in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted cohomology
            %li
              %p
                Grading in cohomology is just one incarnation of twist. Hence the fact that the twist changes under duality was already seen above in the ordinary case of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré duality
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            %li
              %p
                For the special case that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah+duality"} Atiyah duality
                identifies the dual cohomology spectrum with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+space"} Thom space
                cohomology spectrum. Then a choice of orientation amounts to a choice of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+isomorphism"} Thom isomorphism
          %h3#ExpositionExamples 5. Examples
          %p
            Here we survey some examples of cohomological quantization. See (
            %a{:href => "#Nuiten13"}> Nuiten 13, section 5
            ).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            The traditional input for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            represented by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi ω
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                    %mo ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \left[\array{X \\ \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\omega}} \\ \Omega_{cl}^2 }\right]
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of closed
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+2-forms"} differential 2-forms
          %p
            The lack of traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            to act
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functorially
            on such data has become proverbial. An old proposal for how to deal with this (
            %a{:href => "#Hoermander71"}> Hörmander 71
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Weinstein71"} Weinstein 71
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            between
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+spaces"} phase spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_1, \omega_1) \to (X_2, \omega_2)
            to be given by
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondences"} Lagrangian correspondences
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+submanifolds"} Lagrangian submanifolds
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X_1 \times X_2, p_1^\ast \omega_1 - p_2^\ast \omega_2 )
          %p
            Observe that such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondences"} Lagrangian correspondences
            are indeed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} slice (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi cl
                          %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\Omega^2_{cl}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagrams"} diagrams
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %msubsup
                              %mi i
                              %mn 1
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 1
                            %mo =
                            %msubsup
                              %mi i
                              %mn 2
                              %mo *
                            %msub
                              %mi ω
                              %mn 2
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ω
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ω
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Z
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{i_1}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{i_2}}
                  \\\
                  X_1 &amp;&amp; {i_1^\ast \omega_1 = i_2^\ast \omega_2} &amp;&amp; X_2
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\omega_1}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\omega_2}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \Omega^2_{cl}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Notice that a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantization"} prequantization
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            is a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi ω
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F_{(-)}}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{\omega}{\to}&amp; \Omega^2_{cl}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Given such for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ω
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_1
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_2
            %em prequantized
            Lagrangian correspondence to be a factorization of the above through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{(-)}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∇
                                  %mn 1
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mo ∇
                                  %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi conn
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi F
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; Z
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{i_1}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{i_2}}
                  \\\
                  X_1 &amp;&amp; \swArrow_{\simeq} &amp;&amp; X_2
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\nabla_1}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{\nabla_2}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{F_{(-)}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \Omega^2_{cl}
                  }
          %p
            This now yields a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}U(1)}
          %p
            Since by the degree of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            this is going to be a 1-dimensional theory, one is inclined to linearize in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo =
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = H \mathbb{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum
          %p
            However,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            does not receive a twist from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \flat \mathbf{B}U(1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ♭
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi GL
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\flat U(1) \longrightarrow GL_1(H\mathbb{C})
                  \\,.
          %p
            This means we could
            = succeed "-linearize" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\mathbb{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondence"} Lagrangian correspondence
            only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            is flat. But since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
          %p
            What looks like a failure here right away, contains in it the seed of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic
            aspect of motivic quantization which controls all the typical examples: if we need to quantize over
            = succeed "-coefficients" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary field theory
            of a higher dimensional system which we can quantize over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
          %p This turns out to be the case, indeed.
          %p
            The canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
            induced by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\pi)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            version of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of fields is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi dCSFields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2dCSFields}(X,\pi)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+2-bundle"} prequantum 2-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo [
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mrow
                                %mn 2
                                %mi dCSFields
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi exp
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo (
                                    %mi i
                                    %msub
                                      %mi S
                                      %mrow
                                        %mn 2
                                        %mi dCS
                                    %mo )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi B
                              %mn 2
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left[
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{2dCSFields}(X,\pi)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\exp\left(i S_{2dCS}\right)}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
                  }
                  \\right]
                  \\,,
            see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+geometric+quantization+of+2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} extended geometric quantization of 2d Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            One finds that the original
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
            is canonically a boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            for this
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            like this:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi dCSFields
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \swArrow &amp;&amp; \mathbf{2dCSFields}(X,\pi)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            This now is canonically
            = succeed "-linearized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ≔
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \coloneqq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+K-theory"} complex K-theory
            spectrum.
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mrow
                              %mn 2
                              %mi dCSFields
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ρ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mi U
                          %mi Mod
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \swArrow &amp;&amp; \mathbf{2dCSFields}(X,\pi)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\rho}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; K U Mod
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            One finds that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \pi) = (X, \omega^{-1})
            is actually a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifold"} symplectic manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi dCSFields
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2dCSFields}(X,\omega^{-1}) \simeq \ast
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi ξ
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mi U
                          %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;\downarrow^{\xi}&amp; \searrow^{p}
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;\leftarrow &amp; \mathbf{B}U(1) &amp;\rightarrow&amp; \ast
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; K U Mod
                  }
          %p
            and encodes an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            A choice of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/measure"} measure
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo =
                  %mi KU
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E = KU
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-orientation"} K-orientation
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+structure"} spin^c structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            step
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\omega)
            is equipped with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+complex+structure"} almost complex structure
            canonically yields such (as discussed there).
          %p
            With such a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-orientation"} K-orientation
            chosen, the pull-push/fiber-integration/index-map quantization is then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi KU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi ξ
                  %msup
                    %mi KU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ind
                        %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mi KU
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  KU^\bullet(\ast)
                  \\stackrel{\xi}{\to}
                  KU^\bullet(X)
                  \\stackrel{ind_X}{\to}
                  KU^\bullet(\ast)
          %p
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index"} index
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+line+bundle"} prequantum line bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            (see there) say that this agrees with the traditional quantization via holomorphic sections of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
          %p
            Hence we accurately recover the modern version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            by quantizing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
            induced from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+deformation+quantization"} formal deformation quantization
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kontsevich+formality"} Kontsevich formality
            had been recognized by Cattaneo-Felder to be secretly given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+function"} 3-point function
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open string
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbation theory
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+sigma-model"} Poisson sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+field+theory"} non-perturbative
            and non-formal (not just infinitesimal) analog of this situation.
          %p
            So far this produces just the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+action"} Hamiltonian action
            of a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stacks"} quotient stacks
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mrow
                              %mo ∇
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi G
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 2
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi conn
                                %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; X//G
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{i}
                  \\\
                  \\ast &amp;&amp; \swArrow_{\nabla//G} &amp;&amp; \ast//G
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)_{conn^1}
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Now pull-push is in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+K-theory"} groupoid K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            and lands in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            %em equipped
            with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#QuantumObservablesAndEquivariantKTheory"} Quantum observables and equivariant K-theory
          %p
            Passing away from symplectic manifolds: among non-symplectic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifolds"} Poisson manifolds
            of particular interest are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structures"} Lie-Poisson structures
            on the linear dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^\ast
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+groupoid"} symplectic groupoid
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi dCSFields
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{2dCSFields}(\mathfrak{g}^\ast)
                  \\simeq
                  \\mathfrak{g}^\ast//G
          %p
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+stack"} quotient stack
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+action"} coadjoint action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            This is in a way a “dictionary theory” that contains plenty of interesting
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbits"} coadjoint orbits
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O} \hookrightarrow \mathfrak{g}^\ast
          %p
            Taken together this produces a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/defect+QFT"} defect
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theories"} boundary field theories
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
            induced by
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}^\ast
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi trivial
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi theory
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↑
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi λ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo ←
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒪
                            %mi λ
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi boundary
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi pb
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
