                  }
          %p
            The higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+propagator"} quantum propagator
            given by pull-push/index quantization through the bottom correspondence here yields the “universal
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#QuantizationOfLiePoissonStructure"} Quantization of Lie-Poisson structures
          %p
            A similar defects-of-boundaries diagram is obtained when we do consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+correspondences"} Lagrangian correspondences
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"}> defects
            ) between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            after all, but now with the latter correctly understood as themselves already being boundaries of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Notice that all this quantizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle"} particle
            at the boundary of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+string"} topological string
            given by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 2d Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            Therefore it is natural to consider instead the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+superstring"} type II superstring
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi \colon X \to \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} D-brane
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q \hookrightarrow X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Q
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi ξ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi χ
                      %mtr
