          %h2#GeneralTheory
            %strong I)
            General theory
          %p Here we describe technical details of motivic quantization.
          %p We first set up some
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#BasicNotions"} Basic notions
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            that we need. Then we introduce the three steps that constitute motivic quantum theory:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#CorrespondencesAndLocalPrequantumFieldTheory"} Correspondences and local quantum field theory
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#BivariantCohomologyAndTheSuperpositionPrinciple"} Bivariant cohomology and the superposition principle
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PushForwardInCohomologyAndPathIntegralQuantization"} Push-forward in cohomology and path integral quantization
                \.
          %p
            Readers already familar with the higher category theory notation that we happen to use may take the following as the lighning summary of the definition: the whole process that we describe is going to be summarized by the following diagram of
