                        E^{\bullet + \chi_2}(\ast, X_2) \simeq E_{\bullet + \chi_2}(X_2)
                        \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
              is a model for bivariant twisted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
              over
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
              (hence 1-truncated suitably representable objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#TuXuLG03"} Tu-Xu-LG 03
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "#JoachimStolz09"} Joachim-Stolz 09, around p. 4
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi KK
