          %h5#TheClassicalActionFunctionalPrequantizesHamiltonianCorrespondences The classical action functional prequantizes Hamiltonian correspondences
          %p
            The natural question now is which Hamiltonian correspondences may be prequantized and what the corresponding prequantum data is. The following proposition shows that the prequantization of the Hamiltonian correspondence given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is given by the exponentiated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            associated with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Legendre+transform"} Legendre transform
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi p
                    %mo −
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L = p \frac{\partial H}{\partial p} - H
          %p
            Of course all the ingredients in the statement and in the proof od the following proposition are classical. But the notion of prequantized Lagrangian correspondence serves to neatly unify these ingredients and give them a natural place in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            which later naturally leads to the formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantum+geometry"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+prequantum+field+theory"} local prequantum field theory
            and its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"} motivic quantization
          #HamiltonianCorrespondenceIsPrequantizedByTheExponentiatedAction.num_prop
