          %p
            This is discussed in detail at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#geometric+quantization#QuantumStates"} geometric quantization – quantum states
          %h6#QuantumObservablesAndEquivariantKTheory Quantum observables and equivariant K-theory
          %p
            We now discuss how the traditional quantization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+manifolds"} symplectic manifolds
            is reproduced by motivic quantization of the symplectic manifold regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            of its Poisson-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+Chern-Simons+theory"}> 2d Chern-Simons theory
            \.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
