                    \\,.
          %p
            On the level of de Rham cocycles essentially this was observed in (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahBott84"}> Atiyah-Bott 84, prop 6.18
            ).
          %p
            If follows that with a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian+action"} Hamiltonian action
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+operators"} prequantum operators
            given, the
            %a{:href => "#GeometricQuantizationOfSymplecticManifolds"} above situation
            refines to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane"} brane
            that is given by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+groupoids"} action groupoids
            of the following form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
