              %p
                By the discussion in (
                %a{:href => "#FSS09"}> FSS 09
                ) this is to be called the twisted
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string%5Ec+structure"} string^c structure
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mn 2
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{p}_1(Q) \simeq 2 \mathbf{a}|Q
                on
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
          %p
            This data is summarized as constituting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
            for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+field+theory"} boundary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+field+theory"} prequantum field theory
            in dimensions 2, 3 as follows:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Q
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo ↘
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ⇙
                            %mi ξ
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mi χ
                                %mo ≃
                                %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mn 1
                                    %mn 2
                                %msub
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi X
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi a
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
