                  }
          %h5#TheWittenGenus The Witten genus
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            indeed vanishes on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi a
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi Q
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\mathbf{a}|_Q \simeq 0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"} push-forward in generalized cohomology
            to the point exists in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi tmf
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi tmf
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  tmf^\bullet(Q) \to tmf^\bullet(\ast)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi tmf
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(tmf^\bullet(\ast))
            is the ring of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+modular+forms"} topological modular forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+super+conformal+field+theory"} 2d super conformal field theory
            in dependence of the modulus of the conformal torus
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
            of the heterotic string, called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
          %p
            More generally, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\mathbf{a}
            does not vanish but is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cup+product"} cup product
            square of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            = succeed "))." do
              %a{:href => "#ChenHanZhang10"} Chen-Han-Zhang 10
          %h5#TheO9PlaneCharge The M9-brane charge
          %p
            By (
            %a{:href => "#ABG"}> ABG, (11.2)
            ) we have:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_15 Proposition
            %p
              In the
              %a{:href => "#HeteroticStringAtBoundaryOfMembrane"} above situation
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/push-forward+in+generalized+cohomology"} push-forward
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
              goes form the untwisted
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              to the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-2a)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi tmf
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi tmf
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    tmf^\bullet(Q) \to tmf^\bullet(X)_{-2\mathbf{a}}
                    \\,.
          %p
            This perspective on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+anomaly+cancellation"} Green-Schwarz anomaly cancellation
            condition in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation+in+generalized+cohomology"} orientation
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+cohomology"} twisted
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
            originates in (
            %a{:href => "#Sati10"}> Sati 10
            ).
          %p
            By analogy with the above discussion of
            %em
              %a{:href => "#DBraneCharge"} D-brane charge
            the image of this map might be called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mn 9
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M9
                \-brane charge
          %h4#the_boundary_of_3d_chernsimons_theory The boundary of 3d Chern-Simons theory
          %p (…)
          %p
            According to (
            %a{:href => "Chern-Simons%20theory#Witten"}> Witten 89, around (2.20)
            ) the regularization of ordinary
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            involves coupling it so an
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-framing"} 2-framing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{1}{2}p_1
            vanishes .
          %p
            We are thus in a situation similar to that of the membrane theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HeteroticStringAtBoundaryOfMembrane"} above
          %p (…)
          %h2#References References
